---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site, pricing } from '../config/site';

/**
 * ⚠️ Have this reviewed by a Colorado attorney before publishing.
 *
 * Section 3 must stay word-for-word consistent with the cancellation copy on
 * /pricing. There is deliberately NO refund, money-back, or guarantee language
 * anywhere: the offer is a genuine month-to-month trial, and the setup fee is
 * one-time and non-refundable once the work has been done.
 */
const updated = 'July 31, 2026';
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of Service | Rocky Mountain Booking"
  description="The terms governing AI phone answering and appointment booking provided by Rocky Mountain Booking, LLC. Month to month, thirty days' notice, no early termination fee."
  path="/terms"
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated={updated}
  intro={`These terms govern the service ${site.legalName} ("we", "us") provides to you ("Client"). By purchasing or using the service you agree to them.`}
>
  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>Depending on what has been set up for you, the service includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Answering inbound calls to a number you designate, 24 hours a day</li>
    <li>Answering common questions using information you supply</li>
    <li>Booking appointments to a calendar you designate</li>
    <li>Sending SMS appointment confirmations and reminders</li>
    <li>Sending review request messages after completed appointments (Review Bot)</li>
    <li>Transferring calls identified as urgent to a number you designate</li>
    <li>Forwarding calls to your phone automatically if the system is unavailable</li>
    <li>Setup, configuration, and ongoing support</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    SMS features become active on completion of carrier registration, which may happen after the
    service otherwise goes live.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Setup</h2>
  <p>
    A one-time setup fee of ${pricing.setup} is charged before configuration begins. Setup usually
    takes about a week from the initial call and needs your reasonable cooperation: business
    details, call handling preferences, calendar access, and availability for a review call. The
    setup fee covers work performed and is <strong>not refundable</strong> once configuration has
    begun.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Term, billing, and cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>The service is month to month from day one.</strong> There is no long-term contract and
    no minimum term. Monthly fees are billed in advance from the date the service goes live.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>
      Except as set out under &ldquo;Initial thirty days&rdquo; below, either party may cancel at
      any time with thirty (30) days&rsquo; written notice, for any reason or none.
    </strong>{' '}
    Notice may be sent by email to the address at the end of these terms. There is{' '}
    <strong>no early termination fee</strong>. After the initial period described below, service
    continues through the end of the notice period and that final month is payable. Fees already
    paid are not returned, and the setup fee is not refundable.
  </p>

  <h3>Initial thirty days</h3>
  <p>
    Cancellation during the first thirty (30) days following go-live is effective on written notice,
    and <strong>no further monthly fees are due</strong>. The thirty (30) day notice requirement
    above applies after that initial period. Setup fees remain non-refundable in all cases.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>You keep every appointment the service booked for you.</strong> Appointment and contact
    records belong to you, and on cancellation we will export them and release any number we hold on
    your behalf within seven (7) days of your request.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The rate you start at is the rate you keep.</strong> Your monthly rate does not change
    for as long as your service runs continuously. If we raise prices for new clients, that does not
    affect you. Current rate is ${pricing.current} per month against a standard rate of ${
      pricing.standard
    } per month.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may suspend the service if fees are more than 10 days overdue, after notice and a reasonable
    chance to pay.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Giving us accurate information about your business, services, hours and pricing</li>
    <li>Telling us what counts as an urgent call for you</li>
    <li>Maintaining your own phone service, calendar, and any accounts we connect to</li>
    <li>Reviewing booked appointments and responding to transferred urgent calls</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Consent for contacts you supply</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>
      You are solely responsible for obtaining and maintaining any legally required consent from
      people whose contact details you provide to us.
    </strong>{' '}
    That includes consent required under the Telephone Consumer Protection Act, state messaging
    laws, and carrier rules. You confirm you have that consent, that you will honour opt-out
    requests promptly, and you indemnify us against claims arising from a failure to do so.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Reviews</h2>
  <p>
    Review requests are sent to every customer after a completed appointment, with no screening and
    nothing offered in exchange. We will not configure the service to filter by sentiment, to route
    dissatisfied customers away from a public review, or to incentivise reviews, because those
    practices breach Google&rsquo;s policies and the FTC Consumer Review Rule.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not control what customers write, whether they write at all, or what any review platform
    does with a review. We make no representation about the number, rating, or content of reviews
    you will receive.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    The service may not be used for unlawful, deceptive or harassing purposes, for unsolicited
    marketing or robocalling, or in any way that breaches carrier rules or messaging regulations. We
    may suspend or terminate immediately for a breach of this section.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We will use <strong>commercially reasonable efforts</strong> to keep the service running and to
    respond promptly to problems you report. The service depends on third-party telephony,
    messaging, calendar and hosting providers as well as your own phone and internet service.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not offer a guaranteed uptime percentage or a service level agreement.</strong> If
    the system is unavailable, calls forward to the phone number you designated.
  </p>

  <h2>8. No guarantee of outcomes</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not guarantee any particular business result.</strong> We make no representation
    about calls answered, appointments booked, jobs won, revenue, or reviews received. Any figures
    or examples shown on our website or discussed on a call are illustrative only.
  </p>
  <p>
    The service uses automated systems that interpret natural speech. It will not handle every call
    perfectly. It may misunderstand a caller, misjudge urgency, or fail to book correctly. You
    accept this as inherent to the service and agree to keep your own oversight of your operations,
    including for emergencies and safety-related matters.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    Except as expressly stated here, the service is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as
    available&rdquo;, without warranties of any kind, express, implied or statutory, including
    implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      Our total aggregate liability arising out of or relating to the service will not exceed the
      total fees you actually paid us in the three (3) months immediately before the event giving
      rise to the claim.
    </strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    We are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary or punitive
    damages, or for lost profits, revenue, business, data, or missed opportunities, even if advised
    of the possibility.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing here limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited, including for fraud, wilful
    misconduct, or gross negligence.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Confidentiality and data</h2>
  <p>
    Each party will protect the other&rsquo;s non-public business information with reasonable care.
    We retain ownership of the systems, configurations, prompts and tooling used to deliver the
    service. You retain ownership of your business information, customer data, call records and
    appointment data. Our handling of personal information is described in our{' '}
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which forms part of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Termination for breach</h2>
  <p>
    Either party may terminate immediately if the other materially breaches these terms and does not
    cure within 15 days of written notice. On termination we disable the service and you should
    redirect your number. Fees accrued up to termination remain payable.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. Material changes take effect 30 days after we post or notify them.
    Continuing to use the service after that means you accept the revised terms; if you do not, you
    may cancel under section 3.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Colorado, without regard to conflict of
    laws rules. The parties submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts in
    El Paso County, Colorado, and agree to attempt to resolve any dispute in good faith first.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Website content and accessibility</h2>
  <p>
    Information on this website, including pricing and comparisons, is general information and may
    change. Figures used in examples are illustrative and are not quotes. Nothing on this site is an
    offer capable of acceptance until confirmed in writing.
  </p>
  <p>
    We aim to keep this site usable with a keyboard, with a screen reader, and at increased zoom,
    and we work toward WCAG 2.1 AA. If you have difficulty using any part of it, contact us and we
    will help directly and work to fix it.
  </p>

  <h2>16. General</h2>
  <p>
    If any provision is unenforceable the rest remain in effect. Failure to enforce a provision is
    not a waiver. You may not assign these terms without our written consent. These terms, with the
    Privacy Policy, SMS Terms and any written order, are the entire agreement about the service.
  </p>
</Legal>
